      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Row 99, winter daphne. Care: NC State, Missouri BG and RHS agree on part shade to sun, moist but sharply drained soil, shelter and a short, fussy life (NC State: often only 3 or 4 years; Missouri BG: dies suddenly for no clear reason). Conflict on watering: NC State says it can dry out between waterings, Missouri BG says do not let the soil dry out; the dry-top style is kept with a guess interval. Size: RHS 1 to 1.5 m, NC State 3 to 6.5 ft by 2 to 4 ft, Missouri BG 3 to 4 ft; 150 by 150 cm is the RHS upper figure. Hardiness H4 is the RHS rating (Missouri BG: hardy to about -12 C, zone 7). Growth rate not stated, left unknown. Toxicity: NC State grades poison severity high, symptoms unknown, suspected principle mezerein, and notes contact dermatitis; RHS: toxic if eaten, skin irritant, toxic to pets. Severity 3 for ingestion (people), 2 for skin and 2 for cats and dogs are the agent's mapping; symptoms are left empty because no source lists them. No ASPCA page was found for it. Es and it names are machine drafts."
      },
